			"notes": "```yaml\nChanges:\n  - Rewrote basically the entire mod.\n  - Commands are now placed on cooldown based on their success.\n    - Commands that return <= 0 will no longer be placed on cooldown.\n    - Commands that errored were never placed on cooldown.\n  - Rewrote the storage system to use flatfile or db over LuckPerms meta.\n    - The storage type can be changed in the config.yml. \n      - You may need to refresh your config to see these options. Without, it is defaulted to YAML.\n    - Luckperms failed to expire the cooldowns in a way that works 100% of the time.\n      - This caused the time left to show negative numbers, which is now fixed.\n    - Legacy cooldowns (cooldowns started before this version) will still be respected.\n      - The legacy adapter will be removed in 2.1, when I swap my mappings.\n    - This does mean that if you're using the MARIADB storage type, cooldowns will be better respected cross-server.\n```"
		},
